        "title": "Dye Chemistry: Chromophores, Auxochromes, Fiber-Dye Bonding, Fastness",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Color in dyes is quantum mechanical: the molecule absorbs photons at specific wavelengths because the energy gap between molecular orbital levels matches the photon energy. The part of the molecule doing this is the chromophore (the pi-conjugated system). Auxochromic groups modify the absorption wavelength and provide bonding sites. The bond between dye and fiber determines fastness."
